(3372645, 468206, 30049, '<td valign="top">I''m sorry, but what connection does this have with ''School Days''?  I like the silhouette approach and the use of backlighting to highlight the bg is good, although if she were a little farther in front you''d have less light spillover on her shoulders, fingers, and cheek.  An ironed background would help keep the viewer from being distracted.  All JMO of course. :D  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I''m sorry, but what connection does this have with ''School Days''?  I like the silhouette approach and the use of backlighting to highlight the bg is good, although if she were a little farther in front you''d have less light spillover on her shoulders, fingers, and cheek.  An ironed background would help keep the viewer from being distracted.  All JMO of course. :D  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-02-16 12:52:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3372646, 466687, 66524, '<td valign="top">Great expression on the girl''s face.  The glasses are not at all distracting.  I also like the hair - typical if the age group 4th or 5th grade?...I wish there was another angle without so much background, but then if you had to choose from the shots you took, I see why this was entered.  Upon walking away, the background does not take away at all (I always walk away from a photo for a fresh look).  In fact, it adds to the sense of "school" the sense of which is not really represented among the entries.</td>', 'Great expression on the girl''s face.  The glasses are not at all distracting.  I also like the hair - typical if the age group 4th or 5th grade?...I wish there was another angle without so much background, but then if you had to choose from the shots you took, I see why this was entered.  Upon walking away, the background does not take away at all (I always walk away from a photo for a fresh look).  In fact, it adds to the sense of "school" the sense of which is not really represented among the entries.', '2007-02-16 12:52:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3372654, 467847, 30049, '<td valign="top">I get the idea, but it feels like you went a bit overboard with the "MIx" - it''s coming across as cluttered IMO.  Some bounced fill light would help reduce the shadows some, and just a bit more contrast might help as well.  All JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I get the idea, but it feels like you went a bit overboard with the "MIx" - it''s coming across as cluttered IMO.  Some bounced fill light would help reduce the shadows some, and just a bit more contrast might help as well.  All JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-02-16 12:55:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(3372662, 468568, 30049, '<td valign="top">I understand your wanting to use a plain background, that''s a good choice, however, the subject is too close to the wall and the light is casting some harsh shadows.  Just a thought.  Good luck.  BTW - You''re right about the young minds learning quickly!  :D</td>', 'I understand your wanting to use a plain background, that''s a good choice, however, the subject is too close to the wall and the light is casting some harsh shadows.  Just a thought.  Good luck.  BTW - You''re right about the young minds learning quickly!  :D', '2007-02-16 12:57:16.000000', NULL, 1),
