(3384738, 467563, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like how you''ve kept this from being another static image of musical instruments/items by allowing a little motion blur to come into play.  School days connection?  Could go either way I suppose.  This would have been a home run if the pencil holder was a child''s hand - as is, it''s somewhere between a double and triple.  :P  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I like how you''ve kept this from being another static image of musical instruments/items by allowing a little motion blur to come into play.  School days connection?  Could go either way I suppose.  This would have been a home run if the pencil holder was a child''s hand - as is, it''s somewhere between a double and triple.  :P  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-02-20 10:12:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3384747, 465239, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is a nice photo, in a street photo kind of way.  Tells a story, engages the viewer.  The B/W tonal range is very well covered.  Compositionally I think the subject is too centered with the image having a horizontal split.  Pull up the bottom, trim in the right a tad...?  Just a thought.  As for the challenge - what''s the connection to the School Days theme?</td>', 'This is a nice photo, in a street photo kind of way.  Tells a story, engages the viewer.  The B/W tonal range is very well covered.  Compositionally I think the subject is too centered with the image having a horizontal split.  Pull up the bottom, trim in the right a tad...?  Just a thought.  As for the challenge - what''s the connection to the School Days theme?', '2007-02-20 10:18:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3384760, 467719, 30049, '<td valign="top">The first thing that jumps out at me on this photo is the carpet/rug.  :D  I''m being a little humorous, but seriously, first impressions are important.  The other thing I notice right away is the cool color tone and glare from the light coming in from the window on the left.  Use a reflector to bounce some light back in (white foam board works well) and adjust the color temp (white balance) a little towards a warmer tone.  All JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'The first thing that jumps out at me on this photo is the carpet/rug.  :D  I''m being a little humorous, but seriously, first impressions are important.  The other thing I notice right away is the cool color tone and glare from the light coming in from the window on the left.  Use a reflector to bounce some light back in (white foam board works well) and adjust the color temp (white balance) a little towards a warmer tone.  All JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-02-20 10:24:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3384770, 468692, 30049, '<td valign="top">For a still type photo you did a nice job here.  I light the soft, warm feel of the lighting.  Gold reflector?  The clarinet is well focused.  Not sure about the corner to corner positioning, seems a bit too symmetrical.  JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'For a still type photo you did a nice job here.  I light the soft, warm feel of the lighting.  Gold reflector?  The clarinet is well focused.  Not sure about the corner to corner positioning, seems a bit too symmetrical.  JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-02-20 10:28:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3384827, 467912, 50759, '<td valign="top">My mother was a piano teacher and had that exact metronome.  I remember hating it tick tock while I was playing.  Nice capture.</td>', 'My mother was a piano teacher and had that exact metronome.  I remember hating it tick tock while I was playing.  Nice capture.', '2007-02-20 10:46:48.000000', NULL, 1),
