(3420783, 466796, 23913, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i> Really nice shot, but what''s with the way she''s holding the neck of the violin?  It looks all weird over there. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is odd because its  a right hander''s violin, and she is holding it to the left hand side. (the sides go by the bow hand which is most natural in its motion if it is you dominant hand.)<br/> <br/>so thats a small woops....<br/> <br/>there arn''t many lefty (south paw) violins out there but in all my time playing i''ve only ever none one lefty who played his violin backward instead of getting a custom or learning the right hand side. But still he had the chin rest moved to the propper side.<br/> <br/>anyhow its a nice image.<br/>   that is obviously the most distracting part to me since i know alittle more (maybe) than you none violin playing viewer. (her right arm also looks slightly burnt to black in spots)<br/> <br/>great sky to bad about the DQ it alwasy sucks.<br/> <br/>_brando_</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo: Really nice shot, but what''s with the way she''s holding the neck of the violin?  It looks all weird over there.   It is odd because its  a right hander''s violin, and she is holding it to the left hand side. (the sides go by the bow hand which is most natural in its motion if it is you dominant hand.) so thats a small woops.... there arn''t many lefty (south paw) violins out there but in all my time playing i''ve only ever none one lefty who played his violin backward instead of getting a custom or learning the right hand side. But still he had the chin rest moved to the propper side. anyhow its a nice image.   that is obviously the most distracting part to me since i know alittle more (maybe) than you none violin playing viewer. (her right arm also looks slightly burnt to black in spots) great sky to bad about the DQ it alwasy sucks. _brando_', '2007-03-01 21:03:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3421498, 465396, 64994, '<td valign="top">Well, for what it''s worth, I understood it...I didn''t come from a background of wealth and plenty either. Take solice in the fact that there a few people that do get it and 75 votes at or over 6 thats cool!!!<br/> <br/>Thanks for the vote in the tree challenge, from the comments I have received I get the impression that a lot of people thought I had Photoshopped the image!!! No it''s just the Oklahoma wind at work, as I am sure are familier with being from Kansas.<br/> <br/>Trust me your not the only one with a weekness at conveying messages photographicly....lol.</td>', 'Well, for what it''s worth, I understood it...I didn''t come from a background of wealth and plenty either. Take solice in the fact that there a few people that do get it and 75 votes at or over 6 thats cool!!! Thanks for the vote in the tree challenge, from the comments I have received I get the impression that a lot of people thought I had Photoshopped the image!!! No it''s just the Oklahoma wind at work, as I am sure are familier with being from Kansas. Trust me your not the only one with a weekness at conveying messages photographicly....lol.', '2007-03-02 00:55:48.000000', NULL, 0),
